  <h5 id=exposing-outlines-to-users><span class=secno>2026</span> Exposing outlines to users<a class=self-link href=#exposing-outlines-to-users></a></h5>

  <p>User agents are encouraged to expose page <a data-x-lt=outline id=exposing-outlines-to-users:outline href=#outline>outlines</a> to users to
  aid in navigation. This is especially true for non-visual media, e.g. screen readers.</p>

  <div class=example>
   <p>For instance, a user agent could map the arrow keys as follows:</p>

   <dl><dt><kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>← Left</kbd></kbd><dd>Go to previous heading<dt><kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>→ Right</kbd></kbd><dd>Go to next heading<dt><kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>↑ Up</kbd></kbd><dd>Go to next heading whose <a data-x-lt="heading level" id=exposing-outlines-to-users:heading-level href=#heading-level>level</a> is one less than the
    current heading's level<dt><kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>↓ Down</kbd></kbd><dd>Go to next heading whose <a data-x-lt="heading level" id=exposing-outlines-to-users:heading-level-2 href=#heading-level>level</a> is the same as the
    current heading's level</dl>
  </div>


