t-dev href=#dom-img-height>height</a> [ = <var>value</var> ]</code><div class="mdn-anno wrapped before"><button class=mdn-anno-btn onclick=toggleStatus(this)><b class=all-engines-flag title="Support in all current engines.">✔</b><span>MDN</span></button><div class=feature><p><a href=https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLImageElement/height title="The height property of the HTMLImageElement interface indicates the height at which the image is drawn, in CSS pixels if the image is being drawn or rendered to any visual medium such as the screen or a printer; otherwise, it's the natural, pixel density corrected height of the image.">HTMLImageElement/height</a><p class=all-engines-text>Support in all current engines.<div class=support><span data-x="" class="firefox yes"><span>Firefox</span><span>1+</span></span><span data-x="" class="safari yes"><span>Safari</span><span>3+</span></span><span data-x="" class="chrome yes"><span>Chrome</span><span>1+</span></span><hr><span data-x="" class="opera yes"><span>Opera</span><span>12.1+</span></span><span data-x="" class="edge_blink yes"><span>Edge</span><span>79+</span></span><hr><span data-x="" class="edge yes"><span>Edge (Legacy)</span><span>12+</span></span><span data-x="" class="ie yes"><span>Internet Explorer</span><span>5.5+</span></span><hr><span data-x="" class="firefox_android unknown"><span>Firefox Android</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="safari_ios yes"><span>Safari iOS</span><span>1+</span></span><span data-x="" class="chrome_android unknown"><span>Chrome Android</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="webview_android unknown"><span>WebView Android</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="samsunginternet_android unknown"><span>Samsung Internet</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="opera_android yes"><span>Opera Android</span><span>12.1+</span></span></div></div></div><dd>
    <p>These attributes return the actual rendered dimensions of the image, or 0 if the dimensions
