  <p>The <code data-x-lt=input id=the-input-element:the-input-element><a href=#the-input-element>input</a></code> element <a data-x-lt=represents id=the-input-element:represents href=#represents>represents</a> a typed data field, usually with a form
  control to allow the user to edit the data.</p>

  <p>The <dfn data-dfn-for=input data-dfn-type=element-attr data-x=attr-input-type id=attr-input-type><code>type</code></dfn> attribute
  controls the data type (and associated control) of the element. It is an <a data-x-lt="enumerated attribute" id=the-input-element:enumerated-attribute href=#enumerated-attribute>enumerated
  attribute</a> with the following keywords and states:</p>

