  attribute must be less than or equal to the element's <a data-x-lt="maximum allowed value length" id=the-maxlength-and-minlength-attributes:maximum-allowed-value-length-2 href=#maximum-allowed-value-length>maximum allowed value
  length</a>.</p>

  

  <div class=example>

   <p>The following extract shows how a messaging client's text entry could be arbitrarily
   restricted to a fixed number of characters, thus forcing any conversation through this medium to
   be terse and discouraging intelligent discourse.</p>

   <pre><code class=html data-x-lt="<label>what are you doing? <input name=status maxlength=140></label>">&lt;label>What are you doing? &lt;input name=status maxlength=140>&lt;/label></code></pre>

  </div>

