  following keywords and states:</p>

  <ul><li>The "<dfn data-dfn-for=form/enctype,button/enctype data-dfn-type=attr-value data-x=attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded id=attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded><code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code></dfn>" keyword and
   corresponding state.<li>The "<dfn data-dfn-for=form/enctype,button/enctype data-dfn-type=attr-value data-x=attr-fs-enctype-formdata id=attr-fs-enctype-formdata><code>multipart/form-data</code></dfn>" keyword and corresponding
   state.<li>The "<dfn data-dfn-for=form/enctype,button/enctype data-dfn-type=attr-value data-x=attr-fs-enctype-text id=attr-fs-enctype-text><code>text/plain</code></dfn>" keyword and corresponding state.</ul>

  <div algorithm="">
  <p>The attribute's <i data-x-lt="missing value default" id=form-submission-attributes:missing-value-default-3><a href=#missing-value-default>missing value default</a></i> and <i data-x-lt="invalid value default" id=form-submission-attributes:invalid-value-default-3><a href=#invalid-value-default>invalid value default</a></i> are both the <code data-x-lt=attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded id=form-submission-attributes:attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded><a href=#attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</a></code> state.</p>
  </div>

  <p>The <code data-x-lt=attr-fs-formenctype id=form-submission-attributes:attr-fs-formenctype-2><a href=#attr-fs-formenctype>formenctype</a></code> attribute has no <i data-x-lt="missing value default" id=form-submission-attributes:missing-value-default-4><a href=#missing-value-default>missing value default</a></i>, and its <i data-x-lt="invalid value default" id=form-submission-attributes:invalid-value-default-4><a href=#invalid-value-default>invalid value
  default</a></i> is the <code data-x-lt=attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded id=form-submission-attributes:attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded-2><a href=#attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</a></code> state.</p>

  <div algorithm="">
  <p>The <dfn data-x=concept-fs-enctype id=concept-fs-enctype>enctype</dfn> of an element is one of those three states.
  If the element is a <a data-x-lt=concept-submit-button id=form-submission-attributes:concept-submit-button-5 href=#concept-submit-button>submit button</a> and has a <code data-x-lt=attr-fs-formenctype id=form-submission-attributes:attr-fs-formenctype-3><a href=#attr-fs-formenctype>formenctype</a></code> attribute, then the element's <a data-x-lt=concept-fs-enctype id=form-submission-attributes:concept-fs-enctype href=#concept-fs-enctype>enctype</a> is that attribute's state; otherwise, it is the
  <a data-x-lt="form owner" id=form-submission-attributes:form-owner-3 href=#form-owner>form owner</a>'s <code data-x-lt=attr-fs-enctype id=form-submission-attributes:attr-fs-enctype-2><a href=#attr-fs-enctype>enctype</a></code> attribute's state.</p>
