   wearing the <a data-x-lt="autofill anchor mantle" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-anchor-mantle-2 href=#autofill-anchor-mantle>autofill anchor mantle</a>, then set the element's <a data-x-lt="autofill field name" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name-5 href=#autofill-field-name>autofill field
   name</a> to the empty string and return.<li><p>Let <var>form</var> be the element's <a data-x-lt="form owner" id=autofill-processing-model:form-owner href=#form-owner>form owner</a>, if any, or null
   otherwise.<li>
    <p>If <var>form</var> is not null and <var>form</var>'s <code data-x-lt=attr-form-autocomplete id=autofill-processing-model:attr-form-autocomplete><a href=#attr-form-autocomplete>autocomplete</a></code> attribute is in the <a data-x-lt=attr-form-autocomplete-off-state id=autofill-processing-model:attr-form-autocomplete-off-state href=#attr-form-autocomplete-off-state>Off</a> state, then set the element's
    <a data-x-lt="autofill field name" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name-6 href=#autofill-field-name>autofill field name</a> to "<code data-x-lt=attr-fe-autocomplete-off id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-off><a href=#attr-fe-autocomplete-off>off</a></code>".</p>

    <p>Otherwise, set the element's <a data-x-lt="autofill field name" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name-7 href=#autofill-field-name>autofill field name</a> to "<code data-x-lt=attr-fe-autocomplete-on id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-on><a href=#attr-fe-autocomplete-on>on</a></code>".</p>
