  <div class=example>

   <p>In the following example, a script checks the value of a form control each time it is edited,
   and whenever it is not a valid value, uses the <code data-x-lt=dom-cva-setcustomvalidity id=the-constraint-validation-api:dom-cva-setcustomvalidity><a href=#dom-cva-setcustomvalidity>setCustomValidity()</a></code> method to set an appropriate
   message.</p>

   <pre><code class=html data-x-lt="<label>feeling: <input name=f type=&quot;text&quot; oninput=&quot;check(this)&quot;></label> <script> function check(input) { if (input.value == &quot;good&quot; || input.value == &quot;fine&quot; || input.value == &quot;tired&quot;) { input.setcustomvalidity('&quot;' + input.value + '&quot; is not a feeling.'); } else { // input is fine -- reset the error message input.setcustomvalidity(''); } } </script>">&lt;label>Feeling: &lt;input name=f type="text" oninput="check(this)">&lt;/label>
&lt;script>
 function check(input) {
   if (input.value == "good" ||
       input.value == "fine" ||
       input.value == "tired") {
     input.setCustomValidity('"' + input.value + '" is not a feeling.');
   } else {
     // input is fine -- reset the error message
     input.setCustomValidity('');
   }
 }
&lt;/script></code></pre>

