  <code data-x-lt=form id=the-formdataevent-interface:the-form-element-2><a href=#the-form-element>form</a></code> is submitted.</p>
  </div>

  <h4 id=resetting-a-form><span class=secno>2026</span> Resetting a form<a class=self-link href=#resetting-a-form></a></h4>

  <div algorithm="">
  <p>When a <code data-x-lt=form id=resetting-a-form:the-form-element><a href=#the-form-element>form</a></code> element <var>form</var> is <dfn data-x=concept-form-reset id=concept-form-reset>reset</dfn>, run these steps:</p>

  <ol><li><p>Let <var>reset</var> be the result of <a data-x-lt=concept-event-fire id=resetting-a-form:concept-event-fire href=https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire data-x-internal=concept-event-fire>firing an
   event</a> named <code data-x-lt=event-reset id=resetting-a-form:event-reset><a href=#event-reset>reset</a></code> at <var>form</var>, with the <code data-x-lt=dom-event-bubbles id=resetting-a-form:dom-event-bubbles><a href=https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles data-x-internal=dom-event-bubbles>bubbles</a></code> and <code data-x-lt=dom-event-cancelable id=resetting-a-form:dom-event-cancelable><a href=https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-cancelable data-x-internal=dom-event-cancelable>cancelable</a></code> attributes initialized to true.<li><p>If <var>reset</var> is true, then invoke the <a data-x-lt=concept-form-reset-control id=resetting-a-form:concept-form-reset-control href=#concept-form-reset-control>reset algorithm</a> of each <a data-x-lt=category-reset id=resetting-a-form:category-reset href=#category-reset>resettable element</a> whose <a data-x-lt="form owner" id=resetting-a-form:form-owner href=#form-owner>form owner</a> is
   <var>form</var>.</ol>
  </div>

  <p>Each <a data-x-lt=category-reset id=resetting-a-form:category-reset-2 href=#category-reset>resettable element</a> defines its own <dfn data-x=concept-form-reset-control id=concept-form-reset-control>reset algorithm</dfn>. Changes made to form controls as part of
  these algorithms do not count as changes caused by the user (and thus, e.g., do not cause <code data-x-lt=event-input id=resetting-a-form:event-input><a href=https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input data-x-internal=event-input>input</a></code> events to fire).</p>

  



