_android unknown"><span>Opera Android</span><span>?</span></span></div></div><div class=feature><p><a href=https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/PageTransitionEvent title="The PageTransitionEvent event object is available inside handler functions for the pageshow and pagehide events, fired when a document is being loaded or unloaded.">PageTransitionEvent</a><p class=all-engines-text>Support in all current engines.<div class=support><span data-x="" class="firefox yes"><span>Firefox</span><span>1.5+</span></span><span data-x="" class="safari yes"><span>Safari</span><span>5+</span></span><span data-x="" class="chrome yes"><span>Chrome</span><span>4+</span></span><hr><span data-x="" class="opera unknown"><span>Opera</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="edge_blink yes"><span>Edge</span><span>79+</span></span><hr><span data-x="" class="edge yes"><span>Edge (Legacy)</span><span>12+</span></span><span data-x="" class="ie yes"><span>Internet Explorer</span><span>11</span></span><hr><span data-x="" class="firefox_android unknown"><span>Firefox Android</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="safari_ios yes"><span>Safari iOS</span><span>4+</span></span><span data-x="" class="chrome_android unknown"><span>Chrome Android</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="webview_android yes"><span>WebView Android</span><span>37+</span></span><span data-x="" class="samsunginternet_android unknown"><span>Samsung Internet</span><span>?</span></span><span data-x="" class="opera_android unknown"><span>Opera Android</span><span>?</span></span></div></div></div>

