    <ol><li><p><a data-x-lt="clear the stack back to a table body context" id=parsing-main-intbody:clear-the-stack-back-to-a-table-body-context-4 href=#clear-the-stack-back-to-a-table-body-context>Clear the stack back to a table body context</a>. (See below.)<li><p>Pop the <a data-x-lt="current node" id=parsing-main-intbody:current-node-2 href=#current-node>current node</a> from the <a data-x-lt="stack of open elements" id=parsing-main-intbody:stack-of-open-elements-4 href=#stack-of-open-elements>stack of open elements</a>. Switch the
     <a data-x-lt="insertion mode" id=parsing-main-intbody:insertion-mode-5 href=#insertion-mode>insertion mode</a> to "<a data-x-lt="insertion mode: in table" id=parsing-main-intbody:parsing-main-intable-2 href=#parsing-main-intable>in table</a>".<li><p>Reprocess the token.</ol>
   <dt>An end tag whose tag name is one of: "body", "caption", "col", "colgroup", "html", "td",
   "th", "tr"<dd>
    <p><a data-x-lt="parse error" id=parsing-main-intbody:parse-errors-4 href=#parse-errors>Parse error</a>. Ignore the token.</p>
   <dt>Anything else<dd>
    <p>Process the token <a data-x-lt="using the rules for" id=parsing-main-intbody:using-the-rules-for href=#using-the-rules-for>using the rules for</a> the "<a data-x-lt="insertion mode: in table" id=parsing-main-intbody:parsing-main-intable-3 href=#parsing-main-intable>in table</a>" <a data-x-lt="insertion mode" id=parsing-main-intbody:insertion-mode-6 href=#insertion-mode>insertion mode</a>.</p>
