  </div>

  <div algorithm="">
  <p>When the steps above require the UA to <dfn data-x="clear the stack back to a table body context" id=clear-the-stack-back-to-a-table-body-context>clear the stack back to a table body context</dfn>,
  it means that the UA must, while the <a data-x-lt="current node" id=parsing-main-intbody:current-node-3 href=#current-node>current node</a> is not a <code data-x-lt=tbody id=parsing-main-intbody:the-tbody-element><a href=#the-tbody-element>tbody</a></code>,
  <code data-x-lt=tfoot id=parsing-main-intbody:the-tfoot-element><a href=#the-tfoot-element>tfoot</a></code>, <code data-x-lt=thead id=parsing-main-intbody:the-thead-element><a href=#the-thead-element>thead</a></code>, <code data-x-lt=template id=parsing-main-intbody:the-template-element><a href=#the-template-element>template</a></code>, or <code data-x-lt=html id=parsing-main-intbody:the-html-element><a href=#the-html-element>html</a></code> element, pop
  elements from the <a data-x-lt="stack of open elements" id=parsing-main-intbody:stack-of-open-elements-5 href=#stack-of-open-elements>stack of open elements</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <p class=note>The <a data-x-lt="current node" id=parsing-main-intbody:current-node-4 href=#current-node>current node</a> being an <code data-x-lt=html id=parsing-main-intbody:the-html-element-2><a href=#the-html-element>html</a></code> element after this
